<?nvs
// ADR 0006's isolate, as a program: `spawn script` runs another file
// in-process with its own arena, sharing compiled code and the parent's
// budget and nothing else.
//
// The five lines this prints are frozen by an exact check in a goal record
// under `data/goals/`; the source is not. The three children live in
// `examples/isolate/` and each exists to be one of those lines.
//
// The paths are written from the repository root, which is where the
// acceptance driver runs this program from. If item 20 resolves a child
// relative to the *entry file* instead (ADR 0104 makes an application an
// entry-file path, and says nothing about this), these three lines are the
// ones to shorten.

// `output: 'inherit'` — the child writes to this program's stdout directly,
// so its line arrives before anything below it. Awaiting first is what makes
// that ordering a fact rather than a race: § 4 of ADR 0072 applies to an
// isolate exactly as it does to a task.
var $hello = spawn script 'isolate/hello.nvs' with(
    output: 'inherit',
);
var $greeting = await $hello;
if ($greeting->ok) {
    echo 'ok=true', "\n";
} else {
    echo 'ok=false', "\n";
}

// `output: 'capture'` — the same child machinery with the other sink. What
// comes back is the child's bytes, and the parent decides where they go.
var $capture = spawn script 'isolate/capture.nvs' with(
    output: 'capture',
);
var $captured = await $capture;
echo 'captured=', $captured->output, "\n";

// Item 22: a child's uncaught throw is a *value* on this side. It does not
// propagate as a throw — there is no `catch` around this call and none is
// needed — because a child that fails may not be able to end its parent.
// The same is true of a limit breach and of a contained panic inside it
// (ADR 0106 § 2), which is the whole point of the boundary.
var $bad = spawn script 'isolate/throws.nvs' with(
    output: 'capture',
);
var $failed = await $bad;
if ($failed->ok) {
    echo 'ok=true', "\n";
} else {
    echo 'ok=false', "\n";
}

// And the line the three above are all in service of.
echo 'parent still running', "\n";
